## Root Cause
The vulnerability arises from directly concatenating user input into a query, which can lead to SQL injection attacks.

## Explanation
The proposed patch uses parameterized queries to safely handle user input. By utilizing Sequelize's binding methods, the user input is treated as a parameter rather than executing it as part of the SQL command, mitigating the risk of SQL injection.

